        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>AHI SIG241 81 Stainless Steel Back Plates and Levers for Patio Doors</b>\r\n<p>\r\nAmerican tubular passage latchset. All stainless steel construction. These latchsets are normal used on patio doors but can be used on gates or other doors with a 3/4\" bore door prep.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nThis set includes 2 Back Plates, 1\" diameter passage tube latch, 2 different strike plates (full lip and \"T\" strike), 8 mm spindle, your choice of 2 levers and mounting hardware. All parts are stainless steel.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Specifications</b> for AHI SIG241 81 American Patio Door Latchsets\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Back Plate Height: 246 mm (9.45\")</li>\r\n<li>Back Plate Width: 54 mm (2.125\")</li>\r\n<li>Back Plate Thickness: 12 mm (.475\")</li>\r\n<li>Back Plate Material: Solid Stainless Steel</li>\r\n<li>Backset: 2-3/8\" or 2-3/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Door Thickness: 1-3/8\", 1-3/4\" and 2\" (please specify for other door thickness)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nAvailable in Satin Stainless Steel plus 14 different PVD coated color finishes. The PVD (positive vapor deposition) technique uses a high vacuum process to implant extremely resistant Titanium ions over the stainless steel base metal. The durability and highly corrosion resistance of the resulting coating surpass that of  stainless steel. We strongly recommend a PVD finish for  harsh environments.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n<b>* Does NOT fit standard 2-1/8\" inch door bore.</b> If you have a 2-1/8\" pre-drilled door the back plates will NOT cover the bore hole.\r\n</p>",
            "seo": {
